CNet-BBS users can type "TOTALS" at any prompt and see just how big
and impressive your system really is...

> Amiga ShareWare HeadQuarters BBS, 1-810-473-2020, 1:2410/207 ...
>
> Totals v1.7 : As of Sun, Jan 07, 1996      Total System Calls:  10,679
>
> Total Users :    808                       Public Msgs Posted: 556,239
> Active Users:    250                       Public Msgs Online:  98,345
>
> Doors Run   :  3,562                       Email Msgs Sent   :  11,119
> Doors Online:     34                       Email Msgs Online :     878
>
> Files U/Led :  8,258 @ 477 megs            Text Items Read   :   3,606
> Files D/Led : 14,099 @ 837 megs            Text Items Online :     361
>
> Files Online:  9,303 @ 526 megs            Phone Lines       :       2
> Space Remain:  8,471 @ 479 megs (47%)      File and Msg Areas:     450

Aligns all columns and inserts all commas.
(Regardless of whether you have 0 or 1 billion msgs/files online.)

Shows approximate space (and files) that can be U/Led before all HD
partitions are full.

Can be run from the CLI.
(You can re-director output to a file for creating valuable,
informative zzzBBSads, for a change.)

Can also be run online.

Add your own custom header/footer lines.

If the numbers displayed by totals.rexx do not seem accurate, you
might need to run CNet's "Pfiles:Maintenance/Count" program or
"Repair_Sub". "Repair_sub" should be run from the pfile-menu (NOT from
a subboard).

CLI installation:
   1) Copy Totals.rexx TO Rexx:
   2) Edit the variables marked as "SysOp-settable", shown below.
   3) Add "alias tot rx rexx:Totals.rexx 0" to your s:shell-startup file.
                                         ^
                 This should be a port # that is already loaded.
CLI> tot
CLI> tot >t:zzzTotals        (A valuable, informative BBSad for a change)
CLI> rx  >t:zzzBBS rexx:Totals.rexx 0
   (You might want to run that as a nightly CONFIG/EVENT DOS-CMD event.)

Online installation:
   1) Copy Totals.rexx TO Rexx:
   2) Edit the variables marked as "SysOp-settable", shown below.
   3) Add the following line onto the END of the list in CNet:BBSMENU marked
      as "2; Available Everwhere":
         TOTals, TS, Total Stats | {#0 Rexx:Totals.rexx}

If you wish to automatically show your system-totals to all callers,
add the line "{#0 rexx:Totals.rexx}" into the files called
"SysText:sys.info" and "SysText:sys.start".

